---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title='Las Vegas Bakery Websites, Free Demo First | NV Labs'
  description="I'm a Las Vegas web designer who builds your bakery a free demo site first. Menu, hours, cake orders. Call or text (501) 413-3386 to start."
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Las Vegas bakeries</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Websites for Las Vegas bakeries, built by a local guy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm Saad, and I build websites out of Las Vegas. Call or text for a free demo of your
        bakery's site. Menu, hours, cake orders, and a phone-friendly layout you can try before you
        commit.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
        <a class="btn btn-text" href="/#work">See live demos</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="live-title">
      <h2 id="live-title">I live here too</h2>
      <p>
        I know how this town eats. People grab pastries before a shift, order birthday cakes for the
        weekend, and look up "bakery near me" when they're stuck in traffic on the 215.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your bakery doesn't show up with clear hours and a menu, they'll drive to the next one
        that does.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="valley-title">
      <h2 id="valley-title">Getting found across the Valley</h2>
      <p>
        Las Vegas is spread out. A customer in Summerlin isn't going to drive to East Las Vegas for
        a loaf of bread unless they know it's worth it. Your site helps you show up for people near
        you and gives the ones farther out a reason to make the trip.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll write your pages so they clearly say where you are and which parts of town you serve,
        whether that's Spring Valley, Henderson, North Las Vegas, or near the Strip. Plain and
        natural, not stuffed with keywords.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="hours-title">
      <h2 id="hours-title">Hours that match Vegas life</h2>
      <p>
        This city runs on odd schedules. Lots of your customers work nights, weekends, and swing
        shifts. I make your hours easy to find, and I'll add notes like "open early on Saturdays" or
        "closed Mondays" so nobody shows up to a locked door.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="orders-title">
      <h2 id="orders-title">Big order season, handled</h2>
      <p>
        Graduations, holidays, office parties, and a never-ending stream of birthdays. When big
        order season hits, a cake and catering request form on your site saves you from juggling a
        dozen phone calls. People send their details, you reply when you're ready.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="phone-first-title">
      <h2 id="phone-first-title">See it on your phone first</h2>
      <p>
        Here's how I work. I build a free demo of your bakery's site and send you the link. You look
        at it on your phone. If you like it, I put it live. If not, no hard feelings. We work by
        call and text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>How do we work together?</h3>
          <p>
            Call or text works great. Tell me your bakery name and city, and I'll send a demo link
            when it's ready.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Can you help me show up on Google Maps?</h3>
          <p>
            I'll make sure your website and your Google Business Profile have matching name,
            address, phone, and hours. That consistency helps Google trust your info. I can't
            promise rankings, but I can make sure you're set up the right way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>My bakery is in Henderson. Do you work there?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. Henderson, Summerlin, North Las Vegas, Spring Valley, and everywhere in between.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's build your demo</h2>
      <p>Tell me your bakery's name and I'll take it from there.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
